' Question: what happens to a running bot when the app restarts, and how does the owner's Resume bring it back?
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md. Drawn by hand, high level.
@startuml 06-restart-and-resume
participant "BotsModule.boot" as M
participant BotRestoreService as RS
participant BotRunner as R
participant "GridExecutor\n(bot's worker)" as G
participant GridReconciler as RC
participant trading as T

M -> RS : restore_all()
RS -> RS : RUNNING, PAUSED --app_restart--> RECOVERING;\nSTARTING --app_restart--> HALTED
note over RS : nothing is placed, and nothing listens\nto the exchange: the order session is closed
M -> G : BotBootRecovery: recover_after_restart(),\nreport what the exchange holds (read only)
...the owner presses Resume...
R -> T : open the order session\n(open_session_for_resume), or refuse
R -> G : resume() (queued)
G -> RC : run()
RC -> T : open orders and order history
RC -> RC : adopt each order's exchange quantity,\nbook a missed fill once, end a missing order
alt the exchange agrees
  RC -> G : RECOVERING --reconcile_ok--> prior state
else a mismatch
  RC -> G : RECOVERING --reconcile_mismatch--> HALTED
end
@enduml
